ot \\dfrac {\\sqrt{3} + 1} {\\sqrt{3} + 1} &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {2\\left(\\sqrt 3 + 1\\right)} {\\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2 - 1^2} &= \\[5pt]\t\n\t\t\\dfrac {2\\left(\\sqrt 3 + 1\\right)} {3 - 1} &= \\[5pt]\t\t\n\t\t\\dfrac {2\\left(\\sqrt 3 + 1\\right)} {2} &= \\[5pt]\t\n\t\t\\sqrt 3 + 1 &\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054501 #edb/ref 1069 "e-18931" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054501 #edb/ref 1071 "Rationalize the denominator of $\\dfrac{6}{\\sqrt{10} - \\sqrt{6}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054501 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0e811568-769f-5e18-9c6c-5594c18330b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054501 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{10} + \\sqrt{6}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{10} + \\sqrt{6},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}-\\sqrt{6}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}-\\sqrt{6}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6(\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6})}{(\\sqrt{10})^{2}-(\\sqrt{6})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6(\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6})}{10-6} & = \\\\ \\frac{6(\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6})}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6})}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054502 #edb/ref 1069 "e-18932" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054502 #edb/ref 1071 "Rationalize the denominator of $\\dfrac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2} + 1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054502 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5a664cc0-30ca-5097-9505-0755963b0f1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054502 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{2} - 1.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{2} - 1,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}+1} & = \\\\ \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{\\sqrt{2}-1} & = \\\\ \\frac{(2-\\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{2}-1)}{(\\sqrt{2}+1)(\\sq